# Generated Microsoft Office binaries (docs/office/) are produced from markdown
# sources by scripts/gen-office.sh — see docs/office/README.md. Mark them binary
# so git never attempts a text diff/merge or line-ending normalization on them.
*.docx binary
*.xlsx binary
*.pptx binary

# Structural ontology graph artifacts (ontology/structural/) were previously
# committed and routed through a union merge-driver (main#855/#856/#871). That
# whole apparatus was retired by main#939: the index is no longer committed (it is
# gitignored and regenerated on demand — see .gitignore / ontology/README.md), so
# there is nothing here to merge. The merge-driver could never have worked on
# GitHub anyway — custom merge= drivers live in per-clone git config and GitHub's
# server-side merge never runs them — which is precisely why committing the index
# made every concurrent PR conflict. No merge= attribute is registered for it now.
